n includes. The Fedwire Funds Service is the connection in scope for FHLB Cincinnati. More on ACI Connetic is at www.aciworldwide.com/solutions/payments-hub.\n\"Advance volume moves with what members need, and the payment behind it has to work every time. Connetic will give FHLB Cincinnati the ability to continue offering reliable payments in an efficient way with industry-leading technology,\" said Scotty Perkins, executive vice president, product management, payment software, ACI Worldwide. \"Our job is the platform. Theirs is the payments, and the members waiting on them.\"\nFHLB Cinc", "publisher": "yahoo.com", "discovered_published": "2026-09-30T10:30:00+00:00", "retrieved_at": "2026-10-04T19:31:53.691850+00:00", "text_sha256": "772c0ee941b069039dafe5db156bb7b82a5e2d3f4b4c6c23dfbfdaa5b79e0478"}
  - fetch_page({"url": "https://www.electronicpaymentsinternational.com/news/aci-worldwide-swift-ledger-to-aci-connetic/"}) -> {"url": "https://www.electronicpaymentsinternational.com/news/aci-worldwide-swift-ledger-to-aci-connetic/", "title": "ACI Worldwide adds Swift ledger routing to ACI Connetic", "published": "2026-09-23T10:15:00+00:00", "text": "Credit: Piotr Swat / Shutterstock.com.\nACI Worldwide is extending ACI Connetic to support payments orchestrated through Swift\u2019s ledger. The company said in a statement that the update brings \u201cintelligent routing\u201d for Swift ledger transactions into its cloud-native payments hub.\nThe capability is intended to help banks process tokenised deposit payments alongside traditional payment types under a single operating model.\nThe gold standard of business intelligence.\nExperience unmatched clarity with a single platform that combines unique data, AI, and human expertise.\nACI said this approach uses existing operational controls, workflows and infrastructure, removing the need to run separate operations for digital-asset payment processing.\nThe update follows Swift\u2019s announcement last year of a blockchain-based ledger. Swift has since said the ledger is ready for initial use, with 17 banks across six continents piloting use cases.\nThe ledger is designed to enable cross-border movement of tokenised deposits beyond a single institution and outside traditional operating hours.\nACI said many institutions are \u201cyet to fit these payments into day-to-day operations\u201d. It added ACI Connetic is intended to place Swift ledger transactions into the \u201csame environment\u201d that banks use to route, monitor, control and reconcile payments.\nACI Worldwide Account-to-Account Payments head and SVP Craig Ramsey said: \u201cDigital assets should extend a bank\u2019s payment capabilities, not force it to build a second payment operation.\n\u201cBanks need a practical way to operationalise tokenised deposits at scale using the people, controls and processes they already trust.\n\u201cWith ACI Connetic, payments orchestrated through Swift\u2019s ledger can be managed alongside other payment flows within a common operational framework.\u201d\nACI Connetic is positioned as a platform that unifies payment types, payment rails and operational controls. Banks can use a single integration to originate, route and manage tokenised deposit payments and traditional payment flows.\nThe platform applies bank- and customer-defined rules to select clearing and settlement paths. ACI said this lets banks balance speed, cost, availability and custom", "publisher": "electronicpaymentsinternational.com", "discovered_published": "2026-09-23T11:15:00+00:00", "retrieved_at": "2026-10-04T19:31:53.691908+00:00", "text_sha256": "a48bf1798c74b4c08a9e1968465f9cae3f5ae079cacdc8f417a7feda674177e4"}
)

